====================================================
PRACTICAL 05 - WITHDRAW ADVERTISED ROUTES
====================================================

TOPOLOGY

        AS65001                 AS65002

     +--------+              +--------+
     |   R1   |--------------|   R2   |
     +--------+              +--------+

      G0/0                    G0/0
   10.1.1.1/30             10.1.1.2/30

      Lo0                     Lo0
    1.1.1.1/32              2.2.2.2/32

      Lo1                     Lo1
   11.11.11.11/32         22.22.22.22/32

====================================================
OBJECTIVE
====================================================

1. Advertise Routes Using BGP
2. Withdraw Advertised Routes
3. Verify Route Removal
4. Verify BGP Table Updates

====================================================
INITIAL CONFIGURATION
====================================================

R1

router bgp 65001
 neighbor 10.1.1.2 remote-as 65002

 network 1.1.1.1 mask 255.255.255.255
 network 11.11.11.11 mask 255.255.255.255

R2

router bgp 65002
 neighbor 10.1.1.1 remote-as 65001

 network 2.2.2.2 mask 255.255.255.255
 network 22.22.22.22 mask 255.255.255.255

====================================================
VERIFY BEFORE WITHDRAW
====================================================

R2

show ip bgp

Expected:

*> 1.1.1.1/32
*> 11.11.11.11/32
*> 2.2.2.2/32
*> 22.22.22.22/32

====================================================
METHOD 1 - REMOVE NETWORK STATEMENT
====================================================

R1

conf t

router bgp 65001

no network 11.11.11.11 mask 255.255.255.255

end

====================================================
VERIFY AFTER WITHDRAW
====================================================

R2

show ip bgp

Expected:

*> 1.1.1.1/32
*> 2.2.2.2/32
*> 22.22.22.22/32

Route Removed:

11.11.11.11/32

====================================================
VERIFY ROUTING TABLE
====================================================

R2

show ip route bgp

Expected:

B 1.1.1.1/32
B 2.2.2.2/32
B 22.22.22.22/32

Route Missing:

11.11.11.11/32

====================================================
METHOD 2 - REMOVE LOOPBACK INTERFACE
====================================================

R1

conf t

no interface Loopback1

end

====================================================
VERIFY
====================================================

R2

show ip bgp

Expected:

11.11.11.11/32 removed

Reason:

Route no longer exists in routing table.

====================================================
METHOD 3 - SHUT INTERFACE
====================================================

R1

conf t

interface Loopback1
 shutdown

end

Verify:

show ip bgp

Note:

Physical Interfaces Usually Withdraw Routes.

Loopback Interfaces Stay Up On Most IOS Versions.

====================================================
READVERTISE ROUTE
====================================================

R1

conf t

interface Loopback1
 ip address 11.11.11.11 255.255.255.255

router bgp 65001
 network 11.11.11.11 mask 255.255.255.255

end

====================================================
VERIFY ROUTE RETURNS
====================================================

R2

show ip bgp

Expected:

*> 11.11.11.11/32

Route Learned Again

====================================================
USEFUL COMMANDS
====================================================

show ip bgp

show ip bgp summary

show ip route

show ip route bgp

show ip bgp neighbors

show running-config | section bgp

====================================================
EXPECTED LEARNING
====================================================

1. BGP Advertises Only Existing Routes
2. Removing Network Statement Withdraws Route
3. Removing Route From RIB Withdraws Route
4. Neighbor Receives Withdrawal Update
5. BGP Table And Routing Table Update Automatically

